From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: thecorporatetractor <marco@azarguard.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:28:16 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 11/16] core: typed mv-expand converts datetime/timespan
 elements; todatetime(dynamic)

'mv-expand TimeGenerated to typeof(datetime)' on a make-series axis gave null:
the axis holds ISO strings, and the typed conversion only accepted a value
already stored as DateTime, returning the raw JSON node (written as null) for
anything else. The standard anomaly idiom
  make-series ... | extend (flag, score, baseline) = series_decompose_anomalies(n)
  | mv-expand TimeGenerated to typeof(datetime), n to typeof(long), flag to typeof(int)
therefore lost its timestamps.

Typed expansion is now a conversion, like the to*() functions: an element may
be held as the target CLR type, as a JSON string (ISO datetime, "01:30:00",
"7") or as a JSON number (a timespan number is ticks, as make-series stores a
timespan axis). Datetimes come out UTC. A value that cannot be converted is
null, never the raw node.

todatetime() and totimespan() also accept dynamic (an expanded axis element)
and their own type, so an untyped mv-expand followed by todatetime() works.
